{"content":[{"c":["NIBHAZ"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The name of a god worshiped by displaced Avvites after they were forcibly resettled in Samaria by the Assyrians in 722 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". They brought the worship of this idol, as well as that of Tartak, with them at that time (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","r":"2Kgs.17.31","rawR":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.31","value":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 17:31"},"). Although purported to be of Mesopotamian origin, this is not likely because the worshipers were Syrian. The word Nibhaz may be a Hebrew corruption of “altar” and hence a reference to a deified altar that was the object of worship."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Nibhaz","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 17:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d37a21411e58738185be4b6811d96bddf8debe04c4d897ed9111b11f08580d18","sourceItemName":"Nibhaz","sourceItemOrder":135,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Nibhaz","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nibhaz","title":"Nibhaz","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}